    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d760">

                <pb facs="1235" n="1221" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg1221"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">864.4016/12–844: Airgram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Huddle</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bern</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-12-08T11:00:00+01:00">December 8,
                            1944—11 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 20—5 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>A–774. American Interests—Hungary—Protection American Property. Legation’s
                    airgram 455 August 2 and previous.</p>
                <p>Swiss Foreign Office note December 5 states Swiss Legation Budapest reports
                    November 21 various agencies of Hungarian Government have on several occasions
                    taken action against private property belonging enemy nationals.</p>
                <p>A representative of the Swiss Legation at Budapest discussed this matter with
                    Minister Bagossy who made following statement:</p>
                <p>The Hungarian Government intends to accord to private property belonging enemy
                    nationals residing Hungary same treatment which is accorded private property of
                    Hungarian citizens residing in enemy countries.</p>
                <p>With regard to special case of an American citizen of Jewish origin Mr. Bagossy
                    added that Hungarian Government cannot permit that such a person has for example
                    the sum of 100,000 Pengoes in cash for he might use it to the detriment of the
                    Hungarian nation.</p>
                <p>In such cases the funds are deposited with the Commissioner of Jewish Property
                    pending its transfer to a blocked account in the Hungarian National Bank.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huddle</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
